{number: 166}
{title: Pass It On}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
It [D] only takes a spark to [F#m] get a fire going,
And [G] soon all those a-[A7] round can warm up in its glowing;
[D] That's how it is with God's [F#m] love,
Once you've ex-[G] perienced [D] it,
You [G] spread His love to [D] everyone,
You [Em] want to [A7] pass it [D] on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
What a [D] wondrous time is spring, when [F#m] all the trees are budding,
The [G] birds begin to sing, the [A7] flowers start their blooming;
[D] That's how it is with God's [F#m] love,
Once you've ex-[G] perienced [D] it,
You [G] want to sing, it's [D] fresh like spring,
You [Em] want to [A7] pass it [D] on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I [D] wish for you, my friend, this [F#m] happiness that I've found;
You [G] can depend on Him, it [A7] matters not where you're bound;
[D] I'll shout it from the [F#m] mountaintop,
I [G] want my world to [D] know:
The [G] Lord of love has [D] come to me,
I [Em] want to [A7] pass it [D] on.
{end_of_verse}
